,"current_statement_sha256":"sha256:f782846454c6beafa26527e49b43af2452c47353c82cfd6a7a4c81cdc65c5d1b","file":"preprints/Nonsingular-systems-of-equations-over-arbitrary-groups-October-5-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":27,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"05a6af87b15c7a68c64ae946912303ab11040c2858f6b01c4e7b881b32a7b318","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Nonsingular-systems-of-equations-over-arbitrary-groups-October-5-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:f782846454c6beafa26527e49b43af2452c47353c82cfd6a7a4c81cdc65c5d1b","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Nonsingular-systems-of-equations-over-arbitrary-groups-October-5-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L27"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nLet $G$ be any group, let $1\\le m\\le n$ be integers, and let\n$w_1,\\ldots,w_m\\in G*F_n$. If their exponent-sum matrix has row rank\n$m$ over $\\mathbb Q$, then the canonical homomorphism\n\\[\n G\\longrightarrow\n (G*F_n)/\\langle\\!\\langle w_1,\\ldots,w_m\\rangle\\!\\rangle\n\\]\nis injective. Equivalently, the system has a simultaneous solution in\nan overgroup of $G$."}
